{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Cue categories for the call listener (docs/agents/CONTRACT.md, 'Call listener'). One file for the app (data/listen/ScamScorer.kt) and the engine (engine/listener/rules.py). Text is normalised (lower case, apostrophes dropped, other punctuation to spaces). A phrase matches when its words appear in order, each fuzzy-matched (1 edit from 5 letters, 2 from 9), with at most one other word between them. 'negatable' categories ignore a match with a negation word within the window on either side, unless the negation and the next word form an exception pair ('nahi to' = otherwise). English, Hinglish (Latin) and Hindi (Devanagari). Owned by agent A; change it together with a test transcript. Types: a type matches when it has every 'all' category and (if listed) one 'any'; the best score is |all| + |any matched| + |plus matched| + bonus, ties go to the earlier type.",
